#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:1
msgid "IR Lower Trace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:3
msgid ""
"IR Lower Trace shows how TileLang's TIR changes as compiler passes run. It "
"transparently captures the IR before and after *every* pass in the "
"compilation pipeline — including the final codegen step that produces C/CUDA/"
"HIP source — and renders a human-readable diff report in the terminal and/or "
"a self-contained HTML page. No code changes are required: enabling a single "
"environment variable is enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:10
msgid ""
"IR Lower Trace is the recommended successor to {doc}`pass_diff`. Compared "
"with the older `TILELANG_PASS_DIFF` tool, it adds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:13
msgid ""
"**Phase context** — each pass is tagged with its pipeline phase (e.g. "
"`pipeline_c`, `phase1_...`), so you can tell which backend stage a pass "
"belongs to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:16
msgid ""
"**Codegen capture** — the final TIR-to-source lowering is recorded, and the "
"generated C/CUDA/HIP code is dropped to disk for inspection or editing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:18
msgid ""
"**Edit-and-recompile workflow** — edit the generated codegen source on disk "
"and rerun; your edits are injected back into compilation (with conflict "
"detection)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:21
msgid ""
"**Per-compilation isolation** — each kernel compilation owns its records, "
"pass indices, pipeline scopes, and report lifecycle. Concurrent kernels do "
"not write into one shared in-memory trace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:24
msgid ""
"**Raw `.tir` dumps** — before/after IR for every pass is written to disk, "
"keyed by phase and pass index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:26
msgid ""
"**Crash-safe incremental HTML** — the report is flushed after every pass, so "
"partial results survive even if the process crashes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:28
msgid ""
"**Enhanced HTML report** — sidebar pass navigation, status dots, phase tabs, "
"`j`/`k` keyboard navigation, `Shift+E` global expand, `F7` manual alignment, "
"dark/light theme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:32
msgid "Observe the Lowering Pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:34
msgid ""
"The simplest way to enable IR Lower Trace is to set the `TL_LOWER_TRACE` "
"environment variable before running your script:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:37
msgid ""
"# HTML report (default when set to 1/on/true/yes)\n"
"TL_LOWER_TRACE=1 python3 my_script.py\n"
"\n"
"# Colored diff printed to the terminal only\n"
"TL_LOWER_TRACE=terminal python3 my_script.py\n"
"\n"
"# Both terminal output and HTML report\n"
"TL_LOWER_TRACE=both python3 my_script.py\n"
"\n"
"# Disabled (default — zero overhead, no patching)\n"
"python3 my_script.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:51
msgid ""
"TileLang reads this setting when `tilelang` is imported and registers a tool "
"factory for future compilation sessions. It does not patch TVM's default "
"`PassContext` or global codegen functions. To change the setting after "
"import, call `enable()` programmatically."
msgstr ""

